l,{\"d\":\"m12 5 7 7-7 7\"}]]}]]}]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"/services/red-teaming/what-is-a-purple-teamWhat is a purple team?\",{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$Le\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-links__a\",\"href\":\"/services/red-teaming/what-is-a-purple-team\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-links__label\",\"children\":[\"What is a purple team?\",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-links__blurb\",\"children\":\"Our provider offered a purple team debrief. Is that a real thing or a rebrand?\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-links__arrow\",\"width\":\"16\",\"height\":\"16\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"strokeWidth\":\"1.75\",\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"focusable\":\"false\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"path\",null,{\"d\":\"M5 12h14\"}],[\"$\",\"path\",null,{\"d\":\"m12 5 7 7-7 7\"}]]}]]}]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"/services/red-teaming/are-we-ready-for-a-red-teamAre we ready for a red team?\",{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$Le\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-links__a\",\"href\":\"/services/red-teaming/are-we-ready-for-a-red-team\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-links__label\",\"children\":[\"Are we ready for a red team?\",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-links__blurb\",\"children\":\"How do we know whether we would waste the money?\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-links__arrow\",\"width\":\"16\",\"height\":\"16\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"strokeWidth\":\"1.75\",\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"focusable\":\"false\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"path\",null,{\"d\":\"M5 12h14\"}],[\"$\",\"path\",null,{\"d\":\"m12 5 7 7-7 7\"}]]}]]}]}]]}]]}]}]]\n35:[[\"$\",\"style\",null,{\"href\":\"envenox-section\",\"precedence\":\"default\",\"children\":\"\\n.sec {\\n  position: relative;\\n  background-color: var(--bg);\\n  color: var(--fg);\\n}\\n/* Grain sits at z-index 1 with pointer-events none; content rides above it. */\\n.sec > .u-container,\\n.sec > .sec__bleed { position: relative; z-index: 2; }\\n\"}],[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"sec theme-deep transition-theme u-section\",\"data-theme-section\":\"deep\",\"style\":\"$undefined\",\"aria-labelledby\":\"faq\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"u-container\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-head\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-head__rule\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"u-eyebrow sv-head__eyebrow\",\"children\":\"Questions\"}],[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"id\":\"faq\",\"className\":\"sv-h2\",\"children\":\"Frequently asked\"}],null]}],[\"$\",\"$L6e\",null,{\"items\":[{\"q\":\"How is this different from a penetration test?\",\"a\":\"A test measures a system; a red team measures your organisation. Do not buy one before the other — a red team against an untested estate finds the obvious vulnerability a test would have found at a lower rate, and you learn nothing about your detection because the engagement ended at the first open door.\"},{\"q\":\"Will you phish our staff?\",\"a\":\"Only if authorised, and the framing matters. Results are reported as an organisational control outcome, never as a league table of who clicked. A phishing exercise that produces blame makes the next real report arrive later, which is a net loss to your security posture.\"},{\"q\":\"Who knows the exercise is running?\",\"a\":\"A control group of two to four people, plus a white cell contact reachable at any hour for deconfliction. The blue team does not know, because that is the entire point. We will stand down immediately on a control group instruction.\"},{\"q\":\"What if you cause an outage?\",\"a\":\"Rules of engagement prohibit destructive actions, we hold a stop-word that halts everything, and the white cell contact can reach an operator at any hour. In nine engagements we have had no client-impacting outage, and we will tell you if that changes.\"},{\"q\":\"Does this satisfy DORA threat-led penetration testing?\",\"a\":\"The methodology aligns with TIBER-EU and DORA TLPT. Formal TLPT requires a threat intelligence provider and a tester that meet regulator independence criteria, and in some engagements that means we act as one and not the other. We will tell you which during scoping rather than after.\"},{\"q\":\"Is the purple team optional?\",\"a\":\"Technically, but declining it is leaving most of the value on the table. A red team report tells you what happened; the purple session is where your defenders learn to see it, and where the detections actually get written.\"}],\"headingLevel\":3}]]}]}]]\n6f:{\"id\":\"403c44504416ed33d4af4350092b655f174641e336\",\"bound\":null}\n36:[[\"$\",\"style\",null,{\"href\":\"envenox-section\",\"precedence\":\"default\",\"children\":\"\\n.sec {\\n  position: relative;\\n  background-color: var(--bg);\\n  color: var(--fg);\\n}\\n/* Grain sits at z-index 1 with pointer-events none; content rides above it. */\\n.sec > .u-container,\\n.sec > .sec__bleed { position: relative; z-index: 2; }\\n\"}],[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"sec theme-dark transition-theme u-section grain\",\"data-theme-section\":\"dark\",\"style\":\"$undefined\",\"aria-labelledby\":\"enquiry-h2\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"u-container\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-rail\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-rail__aside\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"u-eyebrow\",\"children\":\"Get started\"}],[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"id\":\"enquiry-h2\",\"className\":\"sv-h2\",\"style\":{\"marginTop\":\"var(--s3)\"},\"children\":\"Book a 60-minute scoping call\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-lede\",\"children\":\"A technical conversation with the person who would lead the work — not a qualification script, not a discovery deck. You come away with a written scope, the exclusions stated in the body rather than in an appendix, and a day count that we have not padded.\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-note\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":16,\"height\":16,\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"strokeWidth\":1.75,\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"className\":\"lucide lucide-users\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"style\":{\"display\":\"inline-block\",\"verticalAlign\":\"-3px\",\"marginRight\":\"var(--s2)\"},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"path\",\"1yyitq\",{\"d\":\"M16 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H6a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2\"}],[\"$\",\"path\",\"16gr8j\",{\"d\":\"M16 3.128a4 4 0 0 1 0 7.744\"}],[\"$\",\"path\",\"kshegd\",{\"d\":\"M22 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-3-3.87\"}],[\"$\",\"circle\",\"nufk8\",{\"cx\":\"9\",\"cy\":\"7\",\"r\":\"4\"}],\"$undefined\"]}],\"A red team lead, two or three operators, and a dedicated white cell contact.\"]}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-rail__body\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"form\",null,{\"action\":\"$h6f\",\"className\":\"sv-form\",\"id\":\"enquiry-form\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"input\",null,{\"type\":\"hidden\",\"name\":\"returnTo\",\"value\":\"/services/red-teaming\"}],[[\"$\",\"div\",\"enquiry-incomplete\",{\"id\":\"enquiry-incomplete\",\"className\":\"sv-form__error\",\"role\":\"alert\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"Some required fields came through empty. They are marked below — fill them in and send again.\"}]}],[\"$\",\"div\",\"enquiry-email\",{\"id\":\"enquiry-email\",\"className\":\"sv-form__error\",\"role\":\"alert\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"That email address did not look complete. Check it and send again.\"}]}]],[[\"$\",\"div\",\"name\",{\"className\":\"sv-field\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"label\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-label\",\"htmlFor\":\"enq-name\",\"children\":[\"Your name\",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-req\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"children\":\"*\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"input\",null,{\"id\":\"enq-name\",\"name\":\"name\",\"className\":\"sv-input\",\"type\":\"text\",\"required\":true,\"autoComplete\":\"name\",\"aria-describedby\":\"$undefined\"}],null]}],[\"$\",\"div\",\"email\",{\"className\":\"sv-field\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"label\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-label\",\"htmlFor\":\"enq-email\",\"children\":[\"Business email\",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-req\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"children\":\"*\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"input\",null,{\"id\":\"enq-email\",\"name\":\"email\",\"className\":\"sv-input\",\"type\":\"email\",\"required\":true,\"autoComplete\":\"email\",\"aria-describedby\":\"enq-email-help\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-help\",\"id\":\"enq-email-help\",\"children\":\"We reply from a person, not a no-reply address.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",\"company\",{\"className\":\"sv-field\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"label\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-label\",\"htmlFor\":\"enq-company\",\"children\":[\"Company\",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-req\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"children\":\"*\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"input\",null,{\"id\":\"enq-company\",\"name\":\"company\",\"className\":\"sv-input\",\"type\":\"text\",\"required\":true,\"autoComplete\":\"organization\",\"aria-describedby\":\"$undefined\"}],null]}],[\"$\",\"div\",\"country\",{\"className\":\"sv-field\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"label\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-label\",\"htmlFor\":\"enq-country\",\"children\":[\"Country\",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-req\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"children\":\"*\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"input\",null,{\"id\":\"enq-country\",\"name\":\"country\",\"className\":\"sv-input\",\"type\":\"text\",\"required\":true,\"autoComplete\":\"country-name\",\"aria-describedby\":\"enq-country-help\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-help\",\"id\":\"enq-country-help\",\"children\":\"Relevant for data residency and time zone.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",\"interest\",{\"className\":\"sv-field\",\"children\":[\"$L70\",\"$L71\",null]}],\"$L72\",\"$L73\"],\"$L74\",\"$L75\"]}]}]]}]}]}]]\n76:Tdb3,\n.btn {\n  --btn-bg: transparent;\n  --btn-bg-hover: transparent;\n  --btn-fg: var(--fg);\n  --btn-border: transparent;\n  --btn-border-hover: transparent;\n\n  display: inline-flex;\n  align-items: center;\n  justify-content: center;\n  gap: var(--s2);\n  border: 1px solid var(--btn-border);\n  border-radius: var(--radius-md);\n  background-color: var(--btn-bg);\n  color: var(--btn-fg);\n  font-family: var(--font-inter-tight), var(--font-inter), ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif;\n  font-weight: 500;\n  letter-spacing: -0.01em;\n  line-height: 1;\n  text-align: center;\n  text-decoration: none;\n  cursor: pointer;\n  /* ONLY colour transitions. A transform here would break the house rule. */\n  transition:\n    background-color var(--dur-base) var(--ease-out),\n    border-color var(--dur-base) var(--ease-out),\n    color var(--dur-base) var(--ease-out);\n}\n.btn:hover {\n  background-color: var(--btn-bg-hover);\n  border-color: var(--btn-border-hover);\n  /* Falls back to the resting label colour, so no existing variant changes.\n     A variant whose hover fill moves far in lightness needs to move its label\n     too, or the hover state quietly fails contrast while the resting state\n     passes — which is the kind of thing an audit on static screenshots misses. */\n  color: var(--btn-fg-hover, var(--btn-fg));\n}\n.btn[aria-disabled='true'],\n.btn:disabled {\n  opacity: 0.45;\n  cursor: not-allowed;\n}\n.btn[aria-disabled='true']:hover,\n.btn:disabled:hover {\n  background-color: var(--btn-bg);\n  border-color: var(--btn-border);\n}\n\n/* ---- sizes. md and lg clear the 44x44 touch target. ---- */\n.btn--sm { min-height: 32px; padding-inline: var(--s3); font-size: var(--text-sm); }\n.btn--md { min-height: 44px; min-width: 44px; padding-inline: var(--s4); font-size: var(--text-sm); }\n.btn--lg { min-height: 52px; min-width: 52px; padding-inline: var(--s6); font-size: var(--text-base); }\n\n.btn--full { width: 100%; }\n\n/* ---- variants ---- */\n.btn--primary {\n  --btn-bg: var(--accent);\n  --btn-fg: var(--accent-fg);\n  --btn-bg-hover: color-mix(in oklab, var(--accent) 82%, var(--fg) 18%);\n  --btn-border: var(--accent);\n  --btn-border-hover: color-mix(in oklab, var(--accent) 82%, var(--fg) 18%);\n}\n.theme-light .btn--primary {\n  /* On paper, --accent is the DARK copper (#A04F1A) because it has to pass\n     4.5:1 as link TEXT. As a large filled surface that same value reads muddy\n     brown, which is not what the brand is. A fill has a different contrast\n     problem from text: the requirement is on the LABEL against the fill, and\n     ink on vibrant copper measures 6.9:1 — comfortably clear. So the fill gets\n     the real brand copper and the label goes dark. Links and the focus ring\n     keep --accent and stay legible. */\n  --btn-bg: var(--accent-500);\n  --btn-fg: var(--ink-900);\n  --btn-bg-hover: var(--accent-600);\n  --btn-fg-hover: var(--paper-50);\n  --btn-border: var(--accent-500);\n  --btn-border-hover: var(--accent-600);\n}\n.btn--secondary {\n  --btn-fg: var(--fg);\n  --btn-border: var(--border-strong);\n  --btn-bg-hover: var(--surface);\n  --btn-border-hover: var(--fg);\n}\n.btn--ghost {\n  --btn-fg: var(--muted-strong);\n  --btn-bg-hover: var(--surface);\n  --btn-border-hover: var(--border);\n}\n.btn--ghost:hover { color: var(--fg); }\n.btn--danger-quiet {\n  --btn-fg: var(--muted-strong);\n  --btn-border: var(--border-strong);\n  --btn-bg-hover: var(--surface);\n  --btn-border-hover: var(--muted-strong);\n}\n.btn--danger-quiet:hover { color: var(--fg); }\n\n.btn__icon { display: inline-flex; flex: none; }\n37:[[\"$\",\"style\",null,{\"href\":\"envenox-section\",\"precedence\":\"default\",\"children\":\"\\n.sec {\\n  position: relative;\\n  background-color: var(--bg);\\n  color: var(--fg);\\n}\\n/* Grain sits at z-index 1 with pointer-events none; content rides above it. */\\n.sec > .u-container,\\n.sec > .